      "item_id": "i2",
      "verdict": "supported",
      "rationale": "Both full-sentence excerpts cover the August 2024 announcement, the M365 commercial consolidation and the FY2025 CODM reporting. The comparability point is limited to priority reasoning."
    },
    {
      "item_id": "i3",
      "verdict": "supported",
      "rationale": "The excerpts cover all three stated purposes. Dropping 'timely and rational' does not change the meaning."
    },
    {
      "item_id": "i4",
      "verdict": "partial",
      "rationale": "The 093 excerpt stops before the on-premises clause (Windows Commercial on-premises, Office licensed on-premises), yet the statement claims 'cloud and on-premises'. The 'This segment primarily comprises:' excerpt also lacks its antecedent segment name."
    },
    {
      "item_id": "i5",
      "verdict": "partial",
      "rationale": "The growth excerpt stops at 'growth markets', so the claimed condition about adding AI-enabled tools is not in the selected text. The revenue-driver clause is supported."
    },
    {
      "item_id": "i6",
      "verdict": "partial",
      "rationale": "The second excerpt is a dangling 'which...' clause. The Outlook.com/OneDrive communication and storage demand that it modifies is not quoted."
    },
    {
      "item_id": "i7",
      "verdict": "partial",
      "rationale": "The revenue excerpt stops before the member engagement and sponsored-content quality clause that drives Marketing Solutions. That half of the statement lacks selected support."
    },
    {
      "item_id": "i8",
      "verdict": "partial",
      "rationale": "The first excerpt is only a customer-list fragment. It has no subject and does not include the cloud and on-premises financial management/ERP/CRM/supply chain offerings that the statement claims."
    },
    {
      "item_id": "i9",
      "verdict": "partial",
      "rationale": "The 'We compete by...' excerpt stops before the claim that tools 'work well with technologies our customers already have'. The other competitor-category assertions are supported."
